      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "An Event Handler Is a Reaction Contract",
        "statement": "An Event Handler node should be the complete, inspectable answer to \"when this happens, what does this graph do about it\": it declares what it listens to, decides whether the occurrence concerns it, performs a bounded reaction, and reports what happened, all on the node itself.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "plausible",
        "notes": "This idea is about the handler's behavior. Whether a simple Property reaction needs separate Event and Subscription nodes is a different question, explored in First-Class Event Handler Node (github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/event-handler-node/root.node).",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
