        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What an Event Handler Node Should Do\n\nA handler should be a readable reaction contract: what it listens to, whether the occurrence concerns it, what it does, what it may change, and how it reports.\n\nThis idea works out that contract from the handler in the Edge Class Template. Whether simple Property reactions need separate Event and Subscription nodes is examined separately in `github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/event-handler-node/root.node`."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "event-handler-behavior"
        }
      }
    },
